# Renders the [errors] section for the run protocol; empty when clean.
#
# cErrors has EIGHT columns and this used to print two of them. errcode decides
# whether a code belongs in cIgnoreCodes, linetext is the line that was running
# when it happened, and foreign says the failing code lives outside this library
# - a discovery rather than something the script did. All three were collected,
# stored and thrown away here, and only the grid ever showed them.
#
# Two lines per error, because one line with six fields is read by nobody:
#   1: <text> [<location>]
#   <tab>code <n> in: <the line that was running>
# The second line is left out when there is nothing to put in it.
#
# The stack column stays out. It is a LIST - sys(192) whole, not just the row
# the handler used - and it belongs in the grid, not in a text protocol.

#
# Rows with errcode danger are skipped: they are findings of the danger scan, already in the
# protocol as [danger  ] lines. The row number vN stays the grid's, so gaps are expected.
# Rows with errcode ignored were let through by the ignore list of $handleError: counted in ONE
# line at the end, never listed here, never in $errorCount (breakfilter v1, 2026-09-27).

Calculate vOut as ''
Calculate vIgnored as 0
For vN from 1 to cErrors.$linecount step 1
	If cErrors.[vN].errcode='ignored'
		Calculate vIgnored as vIgnored+1
	Else If cErrors.[vN].errcode<>'danger'
		Calculate vOut as con(vOut,vN,': ',cErrors.[vN].errtext,' [',cErrors.[vN].location,']')
		If cErrors.[vN].foreign
			Calculate vOut as con(vOut,' (foreign: the failing code is not in this library)')
		End If
		Calculate vOut as con(vOut,kCr)
		Calculate vLine as trim(cErrors.[vN].linetext)
		If len(vLine)>0
			Calculate vOut as con(vOut,kTab,'code ',cErrors.[vN].errcode,' in: ',vLine,kCr)
		Else
			Calculate vOut as con(vOut,kTab,'code ',cErrors.[vN].errcode,kCr)
		End If
	End If
End For
If vIgnored>0
	Calculate vOut as con(vOut,vIgnored,' ignored by the ignore list of $handleError - rows in the error log',kCr)
End If
If len(vOut)>0
	Calculate vOut as con(kCr,'[errors]',kCr,vOut)
End If
Quit method vOut